- `action(n1, "start procedure")`, `action(n7, "end procedure")`, `action(n11, "end procedure")`: Hallucinated steps not found in the description, which simply states the process "begins by choosing a book" and terminates when users "end the process" or "complete the process".
- `actor(a_default, "Default", [i1, n1, n2, ...])`: Unfaithful actor assignment; the description explicitly scopes the workflow "For buyers", but all nodes are assigned to a generic "Default" participant.
- `branch(b2, AND)`: Incorrect control-flow logic; the source text presents mutually exclusive alternatives ("either view the book details or see a list of new copies. Alternatively, they can also view a list of used copies"), which requires an XOR split, not concurrent AND execution.
- `precedence(n2, n3)` and `branch(b2, AND)`: Omitted documented behavior and broken chronology; the description allows viewing new copies immediately after selecting a book, but the model inserts an unrelated question action `n3` and omits any edge to `action(n8, "view: new copies")` at this decision point.
- `action(n3, "do you want to view book details")` and `action(n5, "do you want to select a copy or view new copies?")`: Node payload misrepresentation; the description frames these as actionable workflow steps/options, not as interrogative system prompts.
- `defines(v1, "do you want to select a copy or view new copies?", {})`: Unfaithful variable declaration; the description contains no decision variables, yet the model introduces `v1` with an invalid empty range `{}`.
- `precedence(n8, c1)` and `precedence(c1, n10)`: Distorted source progression; the description restricts evaluation to used copies ("if they choose to view a list of used copies, they can evaluate the list and then select their preferred copy"), but the model incorrectly converges the new copies flow (`n8`) into the shared evaluation step `n10`.

Structural Check
- [S1] STC11 failed: Each variable definition must have a valid range with at least two distinct values. | Variable `v1` has an invalid range `[]`.
- [S2] STC16 failed: Every outgoing edge of XOR/OR branches must have exactly one guard. | XOR/OR edge `b1 -> n6` has 0 guards; exactly one is required. | XOR/OR edge `b1 -> n8` has 0 guards; exactly one is required.